<title>SPAIN: BASKETBALL-RESULTS IN THE EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-RESULTS IN THE EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>BARCELONA 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of games in the</p>
<p>European basketball championships on Saturday:</p>
<p>Games to decide 5th to 8th positions:</p>
<p>Poland 55 Lithuania 76 (halftime 25-41)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Poland: Maciej Zielinski 15, Tomasz Jankowski 11, Piotr</p>
<p>Szybilski 10, Mariusz Bacik 8, Dominik Tomczyk 8.</p>
<p>Lithuania: Arturas Karnisovas 21, Eintikis Gintaras 21,</p>
<p>Saulius Stombergas 11, Virginius Praskevicius 8, Dainius</p>
<p>Adomaitis 7.</p>
<p>Lithuania qualify for 1998 World Championships.</p>
<p>playing later:</p>
<p>Spain v Turkey</p>
<p>Games to decide 9th to 12th places:</p>
<p>Israel 91 France 84 (halftime 43-48)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Israel: Oded Katash 27, Tomer Steinhauer 19, Doron Sheffer</p>
<p>12, Lior Ardity 10, Shalom Turgeman 8.</p>
<p>France: Stephane Risacher 23, Fabien Dubos 14, Thierry Gadou</p>
<p>12, Yann Bonato 10, Federic Fauthoux 9.</p>
<p>Germany 93 Croatia 100 (halftime 41-59)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Germany: Denis Wucherer 21, Patrick Femerling 17, Henrik</p>
<p>Roedl 15, Ademola Okulaja 14, Vladimir Bogojevic 10.</p>
<p>Croatia: Damir Mulaomerovic 27, Davor Marcelic 14, Josip</p>
<p>Sesar 15, Slaven Rimac 13, Niksa Prkacin 10.</p>
<p>Semifinals playing later:</p>
<p>Russia v Italy</p>
<p>Greece v Yugoslavia</p>
<p>Semi-final result: Yugoslavia 88 Greece 80 (halftime 43-39)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Yugoslavia: Dejan Bodiroga 22, Predrag Danilovic 20, Sasha Obradovic 12, Zeljko Rebraca 8, Nikola Bulatovic 8.</p>
<p>Greece: Evangelos Koronios 14, George Sigalas 11, Christos Miriounis 10, Ioannis Giannoulis 9, Constantinos Patavoukas 8. Yugoslavia to play winners of Italy vs Russia in final.  </p>
<p>Italy 67 Russia 65 (halftime 33-38)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Russia: Sergei Panov 17,  Vassily Karassev 13, Igor Koudelin 13, Mikhail Mikhailov 8, Andrei Fetissov 8.</p>
<p>Italy: Carlton Myers 19, Denis Marconato 14, Gregor Fucka 13, Alessandro Abbio 9, Davide Bonora 4. -Italy to play Yugoslavia in the final (Sunday 1930 gmt): -Russia to play Greece for the bronze medal (Sunday 1715 gmt)</p>
</text>
